+# GitHub issue review — October 3, 2026
+
+Reviewed all nine open issues and their comments through the GitHub API, then refreshed them at 04:20 UTC on October 3. There were no new or changed issues and no comments. Device reports without logs are not treated as reproduced crashes. No comments or issue closures were posted.
+
+| Issue | Evidence and disposition |
+|---|---|
+| [#58 — Tsundoku update](https://github.com/HayaiApp/hayai/issues/58) | The installation listener discarded a newly installed untrusted APK when there was no previously installed version. The trust-list publication and cancellation/retry lifecycle are repaired. The actual production WTR-LAB and Novel Phoenix APKs also reference missing SourceTracker/RateLimited host interfaces; their binary contracts and minification rules are restored. The published WTR-LAB 1.6.12 and Novel Phoenix 1.6.13 APKs appear immediately in Trust, publish real settings/filters, fetch live popular listings, and retain trust/source rows across a cold debug-APK restart. Signed minified linkage is checked during publication. External package installation verifies discovery/trust rather than the in-app download worker. |
+| [#57 — downloaded files disappear](https://github.com/HayaiApp/hayai/issues/57) | The report describes model extraction in “App 2.5.1,” supplies no Hayai version or usable log, and does not identify a Hayai feature. This tree has no downloaded model extraction workflow. A package/version and file path are needed before assigning a Hayai fix. |
+| [#56 — Read from here](https://github.com/HayaiApp/hayai/issues/56) | Identical chapter text caused the speech queue to ignore a newly requested paragraph. Explicit seeks now replace the queue position; ordinary document refreshes preserve it. Focused queue tests cover explicit seeks and refresh preservation; the emulator verifies the shared TTS controls. A live-extension seek stress check remains separate. |
+| [#55 — Max title lines](https://github.com/HayaiApp/hayai/issues/55) | Comfortable cards had a fixed two-line container even when the title allowed five lines. The existing holder now lets that container grow for longer novel titles and sets the line limit before measurement. Compact titles now use the same preference; cover-only mode has no visible title to expand. Dedicated one-to-five-line visual checks remain separate. |
+| [#54 — Tts on continuos reader](https://github.com/HayaiApp/hayai/issues/54) | A completed queue stayed beyond its last utterance when the same chapter was configured again. Playback can restart a completed queue, begin at the viewport, and resume a paused queue. Delayed callbacks must remain bound to the active chapter and main thread. No device crash stack was supplied. |
+| [#53 — Colofull](https://github.com/HayaiApp/hayai/issues/53) | This requests a different light-theme palette, rather than a reader or installation repair. Evaluate saturation alongside contrast in a separate theme change. |
+| [#52 — Auto-translation and bulk translation](https://github.com/HayaiApp/hayai/issues/52) | Existing offline translation work provides a reusable worker, but automatic transitions and chapter multi-selection need cancellation, target-language identity, and stale-result handling as a complete translation slice. Keep the request open for that work. |
+| [#51 — Translation](https://github.com/HayaiApp/hayai/issues/51) | Browse-title/description translation remains a presentation feature request. It needs bounded caching and original-text access without overwriting J2K metadata or starting network work on every row bind. |
+| [#48 — Hayai tts](https://github.com/HayaiApp/hayai/issues/48) | An explicit language choice is implemented in the existing reader sheet and full TTS settings. Automatic mode prefers the displayed translation/source language; unavailable engine languages report a recoverable error. Preference/queue tests and settings navigation pass; every engine/locale combination is not device-verified. |
+
+The additional reports in this task cover extension cancellation, reader idle crashes, source-local gallery searches, editable Novel identity, and continuous previews. The idle-crash report has no stack or reproduction interval; lifecycle hardening and controlled idle checks can provide scoped evidence, but cannot identify an unobserved Xiaomi/Samsung failure.
+
+Validation results and device limitations are recorded in `.audit/j2k-reset.tsv` and the maintenance plan after the implementation batch.
